228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This report presents the outcomes of a Living Lab research project focused on improving decision-making around the redesign and implementation of GOW30 roads in Amsterdam. Following the city-wide introduction of a 30 km/h speed limit on arterial roads, the project addresses a key challenge: how policy ambitions and technical guidelines translate into credible, context-sensitive road designs that support speed compliance, safety, and liveability.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Using a Living Lab approach, the research combines policy review, expert interviews, and a co-creation session with expert stakeholders from government, consultancy, research, and advocacy organisations. The findings show that GOW30 implementation is not primarily constrained by a lack of technical knowledge, but by fragmented decision-making structures, limited shared understanding, and difficulties in communicating design trade-offs across disciplines and stakeholder groups.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The report concludes that such tools can strengthen public dialogue and governance by making complex design decisions more explicit, comparable, and accessible. It demonstrates the potential of combining Living Lab research with digital visualisation using AI-models to support collaborative decision-making. Further development could enhance its applicability within Amsterdam and its transferability to other urban contexts facing similar challenges.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
