/E (First, we listed all relevant stakeholders relating to our topic. Starting with our case initiator, DRO-DMI, we mapped out the Municipality of Amsterdam, AMS institute and Goudappel. Besides Goudappel, consultancy firm DTV have also published extensive research on road design and redesign policies surrounding GOW30. Furthermore, other knowledge institutes that are involved in Amsterdam GOW30 policy and road design are TU Delft, SWOV, and CROW. Finally, civil parties and advocacy groups are related stakeholders as well. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Second, we analysed their power and interest in GOW30 implementation processes. The civil and advocacy stakeholders hold the most interest as they are the most vulnerable road users for whom speed limit compliance of car users is extra important. Then, the knowledge stakeholders have on average slightly more power than civil stakeholders however, some are more specialised in this topic than others. Thus, those with more specialized knowledge are placed with a higher interest on the matrix. The Municipality of Amsterdam has the highest power given that they implement the policy and hold the executive power on this topic. However, the municipality also must deal with all other governmental tasks besides tackling challenges on GOW30 roads, hence their interest is not as high. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
>>
