/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In the Netherlands, roads are commonly paved with smooth asphalt, or with element paving, specifically bricks or clinkers \(klinkers\). The latter type is particularly common on residential service roads \(ETW\) that serve slow traffic in low volumes. The slowing effect of element paving on traffic occurs due to the increased tyre noise and vehicle vibration \(Andriesse et al., n.d.; Loprencipe et al., 2019\).)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
