/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The analysis revealed interesting results; the criterion that was mentioned most frequently by stakeholders was public greenery \(n=6\). After greenery, the most frequently mentioned criteria were parking and traffic intensity \(of both motorized and bicycle traffic\). When comparing the criteria mentioned by stakeholders with the list of 11 criteria as part of the initial design framework, it becomes apparent that the workshop mostly validated the preliminary list. Five of the eleven items were explicitly mentioned during the workshop: motor vehicle intensity, bicycle traffic intensity, parking intensity, and public transport/emergency routes. Additionally, several criteria in the initial framework also aligned conceptually but were worded slightly different by the stakeholders, such as land use, vulnerable groups, and freight/heavy traffic. Given the frequent mentioning of public greenery, this criterion could be added to the tool in the future.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [0]
>>
