534 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Supporting this, representatives from the Fietsersbond strongly emphasised inclusivity: older pedestrians, children, and people with mobility challenges often feel unsafe in environments relying on informal negotiation. They referenced case examples such as Rozengracht and IJ-boulevard, where minimal regulation was meant to induce caution, but instead produced anxiety and avoidance among users. Panel members all agreed this logic cannot be transferred to GOW30 corridors, where consistency, recognisability, and predictability are essential components of self-explaining road design \(CROW, 2023; SWOV, 2019\).)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
