652 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The use of AI-generated visualizations introduces other considerations. Visual scenarios make complex design choices more accessible and help non-designers engage in abstract discussions. Yet, AI-generated images also pose several risks. For example, they might oversimplify spatial constraints or unintentionally misrepresent real-life conditions or reflect biases embedded in logic behind our tool. Furthermore, image generation requires high amounts of energy, hence environmental concerns may appear. To address this, future iterations should incorporate human validation steps, clearer explanations of assumptions, and possibly non-AI visualization extensions. )
/E (The use of AI-generated visualizations introduces other considerations. Visual scenarios make complex design choices more accessible and help non-designers engage in abstract discussions. Yet, AI-generated images also pose several risks. For example, they might oversimplify spatial constraints or unintentionally misrepresent real-life conditions or reflect biases embedded in logic behind our tool. Furthermore, image generation requires high amounts of energy, hence environmental concerns may appear. To address this, future iterations should incorporate human validation steps, clearer explanations of assumptions, and possibly non-AI visualization extensions. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
653 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Lastly, this tool has yet to be applied in realistic situations of decision-making. Future research should be directed at piloting the tool on real-life cases, observing its usage within public dialogues or co-creation session between stakeholders and assessing the impact it may have on decision speed, stakeholder alignment, and perceived transparency. )
/E (Lastly, this tool has yet to be applied in realistic situations of decision-making. Future research should be directed at piloting the tool on real-life cases, observing its usage within public dialogues or co-creation session between stakeholders and assessing the impact it may have on decision speed, stakeholder alignment, and perceived transparency. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
654 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Overall, these limitations do not weaken the relevance of the findings. Many highlight the complexity of governing GOW30 road redesigns and the need for iterative, collaborative design sessions. This project demonstrates that there is a clear institutional demand for tools that help prioritize interventions, clarify trade-offs, and increase transparency. To reach that potential, future research should expand the stakeholder base, add quantitative and financial foundations to the tool, and test the tool in real-life decision-making scenarios. In doing so, this decision support tool could evolve from a conversation starter into useful tool within the governance process and help shift Amsterdam towards higher compliance and more liveable GOW30 roads.)
/E (Overall, these limitations do not weaken the relevance of the findings. Many highlight the complexity of governing GOW30 road redesigns and the need for iterative, collaborative design sessions. This project demonstrates that there is a clear institutional demand for tools that help prioritize interventions, clarify trade-offs, and increase transparency. To reach that potential, future research should expand the stakeholder base, add quantitative and financial foundations to the tool, and test the tool in real-life decision-making scenarios. In doing so, this decision support tool could evolve from a conversation starter into useful tool within the governance process and help shift Amsterdam towards higher compliance and more liveable GOW30 roads.)
/Pg 39 0 R
>>
endobj
